<title>USA: Au Bon Pain Q1 net falls.</title>
<headline>Au Bon Pain Q1 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the 16 weeks ended</p>
<p>						  Apr 19,	   Apr 20,</p>
<p>						   1997		1996</p>
<p>Total revenues			 $71,509,817     $69,440,784</p>
<p>Total costs and expenses	    68,989,973	66,600,816</p>
<p>Operating income			 2,519,844	 2,839,968</p>
<p>Net income				    11,923	   797,340</p>
<p>Net income per common share		 0.00		0.07</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>common and common equivalent</p>
<p>  shares outstanding		   11,805,126	11,821,538</p>
<p>NOTE: Company said that during the first quarter of 1997, it experienced higher interest expense associated with the new debt financing completed in July, 1996, incremental infrastructure costs to support the roll-out of Saint Louis Bread and Au Bon Pain International over the remainder of the year, and a new level of fixed costs associated with the frozen dough facility opened in July, 1996. It said these factors  offset continued extraordinarily strong growth in both sales and contribution at the company's Saint Louis Bread business unit. Full company name is Au Bon Pain Co Inc. --((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
